#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105657 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f8fd8a4-1ca2-521d-8542-d11311bcc586" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variance Using the Definition Given a Probability Mass Function"}] :question/id #uuid "9a5697c7-0aa6-55d9-898c-6e954960df42" :question/math-academy-id "e-7388" :question/problem "Let $X$ be the number obtained by a spinner with four sections labeled $1, 2, 3, 4.$ The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\textrm{Var}[X]?$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The variance of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} (x - \\textrm E[X])^2 \\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\textrm E[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{6})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{3})+4(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\textrm E[X]=\\dfrac{8}{3}$ into the variance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S} \\left(x - \\dfrac{8}{3} \\right)^2 \\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the variance as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & ={(1-\\frac{8}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{(2-\\frac{8}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{(3-\\frac{8}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{(4-\\frac{8}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{9}\\cdot f(1)+\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot f(2)+\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot f(3)+\\frac{16}{9}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{9}(\\frac{1}{6})+\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4})+\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3})+\\frac{16}{9}(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105658 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e448e28-466c-5051-9ada-5e030e6a8ff7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Standard Deviation of a Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "ee9c8798-408e-507a-8205-8f16c672c767" :question/math-academy-id "e-7390" :question/problem "A fair die with sides labeled with numbers $1$ through $6$ is thrown once. If $X$ is the outcome of the die, what is $\\textrm{SD}[X]?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a random variable $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\textrm{SD}[X] = \\sqrt{ \\textrm{Var}[X] },\n$$\n\nwhere the variance can be computed using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E[X^2] - \\textrm E[X]^2\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute the probability mass function $f(x).$ Here, there are $6$ possible outcomes ($1,2,3,4,5,6$) and each outcome has the same probability, so the probability mass function is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ |\n\nNext, we compute $\\textrm E[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{6})+2(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+4(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{6})+6(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $\\textrm E[X^2].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X^2$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4)+{5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{6})+4(\\frac{1}{6})+9(\\frac{1}{6})+16(\\frac{1}{6})+25(\\frac{1}{6})+36(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{91}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{91}{6}-{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{91}{6}-\\frac{49}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{35}{12}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105662 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e6a0c79-9597-5fca-9d41-305c541a7bdf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variance Given a Probability Mass Function"}] :question/id #uuid "fcd99105-cd96-57d0-b5df-b6230f18a181" :question/math-academy-id "e-7415" :question/problem "A fair die with sides labeled with numbers $1$ through $6$ is thrown once. If $X$ is the outcome of the die, what is the variance of $X?$" :question/worked-solution "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E[X^2] - \\textrm E[X]^2\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute the probability mass function $f(x).$ Here, there are $6$ possible outcomes ($1,2,3,4,5,6$) and each outcome has the same probability, so the probability mass function is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ |\n\nNext, we compute $\\textrm E[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{6})+2(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+4(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{6})+6(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $\\textrm E[X^2].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X^2$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4)+{5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{6})+4(\\frac{1}{6})+9(\\frac{1}{6})+16(\\frac{1}{6})+25(\\frac{1}{6})+36(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{91}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{91}{6}-{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{91}{6}-\\frac{49}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105663 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "11b6d79a-b13d-5e77-899d-8b1b91c872b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variance Given the Expected Value of a Random Variable and Its Square"}] :question/id #uuid "f07a0b1e-2b90-5b83-b9e2-a8da0bedf044" :question/math-academy-id "e-7416" :question/problem "If $\\textrm E[X] = 4$ and $\\textrm E[X^2] = 21,$ then what is $\\textrm{Var}[X]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E[X^2] - \\textrm E[X]^2\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =21-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =21-16 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e448e28-466c-5051-9ada-5e030e6a8ff7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Standard Deviation of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "628c0069-f4dc-53cd-aed0-ecb82d580e1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410451} {:answer/id #uuid "7343a751-cd78-5b59-8011-1e74e9d823c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410452} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3fe6f1-6e29-5dfa-896a-f38bb44b409d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410456} {:answer/id #uuid "e169670d-6976-5ddd-bc4f-8bbaef5c24d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410461} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b9a1a2-e3e4-59b1-8b62-123fabfad613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc3fe6f1-6e29-5dfa-896a-f38bb44b409d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410456} :answer-field/id #uuid "54f3e13c-4881-5f73-95a1-cd084b9b5b78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ddfb506-4076-564a-9cbf-01888893404d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129110" :question/problem "Two fair  four-sided dice are rolled and $X$ is the absolute difference of their scores. The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{SD}[X]?$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a random variable $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]},\n$$\n\nwhere the variance can be computed using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{4})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{4})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-{(\\frac{5}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{25}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{15}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369623 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e448e28-466c-5051-9ada-5e030e6a8ff7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Standard Deviation of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6495623-12f7-5d4f-b4c2-d63ba2deba68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369625} {:answer/id #uuid "b5791bc1-3d65-5768-b899-8831e853dab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{87}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369626} {:answer/id #uuid "db0c61d2-480c-5bfb-8d90-5c10bacc23e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{95}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369627} {:answer/id #uuid "afadb1b3-7ae9-5aba-bbe9-102544a7b3d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369628} {:answer/id #uuid "08444327-b52d-580c-ab45-5a9f94b9c892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08444327-b52d-580c-ab45-5a9f94b9c892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369629} :answer-field/id #uuid "d894c694-0d37-511a-b335-35626b26b0c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55c2fb27-330a-5719-80e8-28e86364e50d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129111" :question/problem "Let $X$ be the number obtained by a fair spinner with five sections labeled $-2,-1,1,2,3.$ What is $\\text{SD}[X]?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a random variable $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]},\n$$\n\nwhere the variance can be computed using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute the probability mass function $f(x).$ Here, there are $5$ possible outcomes ($-2,-1,1,2,3$) and each outcome has the same probability, so the probability mass function is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =(-2)\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =(-2)(\\frac{1}{5})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{5})+1(\\frac{1}{5})+2(\\frac{1}{5})+3(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & =(-2)^{2}\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)^{2}\\cdot f(-1)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{5})+1(\\frac{1}{5})+1(\\frac{1}{5})+4(\\frac{1}{5})+9(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{5}-{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{5}-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{95}{25}-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{86}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{86}{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "11b6d79a-b13d-5e77-899d-8b1b91c872b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variance Given the Expected Value of a Random Variable and Its Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "123d88b7-9486-5594-8990-9a41d6aa27a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{50}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410442} {:answer/id #uuid "3e2bbc05-907f-5fa2-9ace-d03b3459805d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410446} {:answer/id #uuid "5dfbb2b0-4850-57fe-8e1c-d722559c182b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{71}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410450} {:answer/id #uuid "c23e1601-7810-56cc-855c-b729ce1acc00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410457} {:answer/id #uuid "f787ac39-f172-5118-a383-007f850a6ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dfbb2b0-4850-57fe-8e1c-d722559c182b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{71}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410450} :answer-field/id #uuid "5db94061-cdf0-57e7-b013-67cd72f1cc89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9682caf0-f7aa-52f6-bd4c-fbe55d6bcce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-84011" :question/problem "If $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{5}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{3}{4},$ then what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\frac{3}{4}-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{71}{100}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "11b6d79a-b13d-5e77-899d-8b1b91c872b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variance Given the Expected Value of a Random Variable and Its Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d72eb555-87d0-5526-9c70-b70568124685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382533} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc07cad-b67b-56d5-8534-d467d9c0a7c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382534} {:answer/id #uuid "406d7ee6-8dea-5d51-b3aa-c2b96136d66e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382535} {:answer/id #uuid "654df0e0-61ef-53de-9102-da25f8f2903e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382536} {:answer/id #uuid "1d735932-5b00-56e0-8bb9-acfa5c8b62f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcc07cad-b67b-56d5-8534-d467d9c0a7c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382534} :answer-field/id #uuid "84dc87f5-6f21-53e1-8126-534a0ac395b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382532}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2b6da3ac-314c-5482-b55b-207ba10d814b" :question/math-academy-id "q-84015" :question/problem "If $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{7}{2},$ then what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\frac{7}{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f8fd8a4-1ca2-521d-8542-d11311bcc586" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variance Using the Definition Given a Probability Mass Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c72d57-b201-5ee3-a487-6244a6d0649a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371182} {:answer/id #uuid "9548b886-d46c-5688-987c-0335cef8df6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371183} {:answer/id #uuid "19558ef8-530c-5912-ae82-aa41fa31a638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371184} {:answer/id #uuid "9b71a5ea-cbbf-5f3b-b8ab-e1131ac7366c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371185} {:answer/id #uuid "bc0f98d1-d3c3-507a-832e-30bfd3f24d9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b71a5ea-cbbf-5f3b-b8ab-e1131ac7366c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371185} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4fed912-665f-598e-b974-487031dfc133" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c57ea478-3423-501b-a85e-7b282c883e9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-84023" :question/problem "Let $X$ be the number obtained by a spinner with four sections labeled $1,2,3,4.$ The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{Var}[X]?$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The variance of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{3})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+4(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{7}{3}$ into the variance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{(x-\\frac{7}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the variance as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & ={(1-\\frac{7}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{(2-\\frac{7}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{(3-\\frac{7}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{(4-\\frac{7}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{9}\\cdot f(1)+\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot f(2)+\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot f(3)+\\frac{25}{9}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{9}(\\frac{1}{3})+\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4})+\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6})+\\frac{25}{9}(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e6a0c79-9597-5fca-9d41-305c541a7bdf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variance Given a Probability Mass Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "575e5eff-9795-532d-93c5-3c4f24b1c8e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{625}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371217} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5a6ab7-e175-52eb-92f6-8419475c61bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{625}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371218} {:answer/id #uuid "3a9658cc-79ce-560a-9358-482ffe196e5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371219} {:answer/id #uuid "1f418941-3f01-59c9-8aa9-66da5a58641f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{256}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371220} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0a4d3f-905e-592e-9ccb-9c89b266accc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a9658cc-79ce-560a-9358-482ffe196e5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371219} :answer-field/id #uuid "f80016c8-d0ec-540f-b9e0-f6708f53835d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "abd64ded-a2d8-5cf8-869f-04f6df4aadad" :question/math-academy-id "q-84207" :question/problem "Let $X$ be the outcome of rolling an unfair five-sided die that follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is $\\text{Var}[X]?$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{256}{625}$ | $\\frac{256}{625}$ | $\\frac{96}{625}$ | $\\frac{16}{625}$ | $\\frac{1}{625}$ |" :question/worked-solution "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{256}{625})+1(\\frac{256}{625})+2(\\frac{96}{625})+3(\\frac{16}{625})+4(\\frac{1}{625}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(4)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(5) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{256}{625})+1(\\frac{256}{625})+4(\\frac{96}{625})+9(\\frac{16}{625})+16(\\frac{1}{625}) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{25}-{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{25}-\\frac{16}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
